talk(561,'1982-09-06','A. A. Kirillov','P001026-P001031','Affine sl(2), the principal Heisenberg algebra, and vertex operators',r'Kirillov explains the Lepowsky--Wilson realization of the basic affine \(\mathfrak{sl}_2\)-module. Gelfand interrupts with generators and relations, root monomials, Heisenberg subalgebras and possible analogies with paths, \(p\)-adic algebra and quadratic forms. The actual mathematical entry occupies P001026--P001029; the catalogue range overlaps Zamolodchikov, whose heading begins P001030. The loop cocycle, central generator and oscillator indices require explicit normalization corrections. The 1978 published construction makes the principal line expository in September 1982.')
add(561,'Cartan generators and the Serre quotient','P001026-P001027','construction',r'Generators \(e_i,h_i,f_i\) satisfy \([e_i,f_j]=\delta_{ij}h_i\), \([h_i,e_j]=a_{ij}e_j\), \([h_i,f_j]=-a_{ij}f_j\), and commuting \(h_i\). Gelfand says \ru{Корней можно не учить}. The extra relations are written as ordinary powers, and the off-diagonal inequality is strict.',r'For a generalized Cartan matrix \(A\), require \(a_{ii}=2\), \(a_{ij}\in\mathbb Z_{\le0}\) for \(i\ne j\), and \(a_{ij}=0\iff a_{ji}=0\). The derived Kac--Moody algebra is generated by these elements subject to the displayed brackets and \((\operatorname{ad}e_i)^{1-a_{ij}}e_j=(\operatorname{ad}f_i)^{1-a_{ij}}f_j=0\), \(i\ne j\). Root vectors are obtained from iterated Lie brackets, not associative products.',r'The finite-growth construction predates the talk: \citet[Chapter II]{kac1968graded}; the standard presentation is organized in \citet[Chapter 1]{kac1983infinite}. The notebook compresses several statements into an informal uniqueness assertion.',('kac1968graded','kac1983infinite'),literal='false as written',reconstruction='The generalized Cartan conditions, adjoint notation, and distinction between the derived algebra and its Cartan extension are editorial qualifications.',speaker='I. M. Gelfand')
add(561,'Finite and affine types and the rank-two examples','P001027-P001028','theorem',r'Finite-dimensionality is identified with \(A>0\); affine type with \(A\ge0\), rank \(n-1\). Rank-two examples are \(A_2,B_2,G_2\). The first affine matrix is written \(\left(\begin{smallmatrix}2&-2\\-2&-2\end{smallmatrix}\right)\), then corrected implicitly in Kirillov\textquotesingle s repetition.',r'For an indecomposable symmetrizable generalized Cartan matrix \(A\), choose positive diagonal \(D\) with \(DA\) symmetric. Finite type is equivalent to positive definiteness of \(DA\); affine type to positive semidefiniteness of corank one. The affine matrices here are \(\left(\begin{smallmatrix}2&-2\\-2&2\end{smallmatrix}\right)\) and \(\left(\begin{smallmatrix}2&-4\\-1&2\end{smallmatrix}\right)\).',r'Finite/affine classification is old material in \citet[Chapter II]{kac1968graded}; \citet[Chapter 4]{kac1983infinite} gives the generalized Cartan formulation. Positivity of a nonsymmetric matrix requires interpretation.',('kac1968graded','kac1983infinite'),literal='false as written',reconstruction='Indecomposability, symmetrizability and the positive diagonal symmetrizer are added; the lower-right affine entry is emended to +2.')
add(561,'The Heisenberg central extension of a symplectic space','P001028','definition',r'\(E\oplus\mathbb R\mathbf1\), with \([x,y]=\langle x,y\rangle\mathbf1\), is introduced as the Heisenberg algebra.',r'If \((E,\omega)\) is a real symplectic vector space, define \([(x,a),(y,b)]=(0,\omega(x,y))\). Bilinearity, antisymmetry and centrality give a Lie algebra; for finite-dimensional nondegenerate \(E\) its center is exactly \(\mathbb R\mathbf1\).',r'This is the standard central-extension model underlying the oscillator realization in \citet[pp.~43--53]{lepowskywilson1978construction}; the definition itself needs no conjectural step.',('lepowskywilson1978construction',),literal='correct',match='partial',reconstruction='Nondegeneracy and the finite-dimensional qualification for the center are explicit here.')
add(561,'Loop realization and the sign of the central cocycle','P001028','construction',r'The notes use \([A,B]=AB-BA+\operatorname{Res}\operatorname{tr}(A\,dB)\mathbf1\), with \(e_1=E_{12}\), \(f_1=E_{21}\), \(e_2=tE_{21}\), \(f_2=t^{-1}E_{12}\), and \(h_2=-h_1+\mathbf1\).',r'On \(\mathfrak{sl}_2(\mathbb C[t,t^{-1}])\oplus\mathbb C K\), the cocycle \(\operatorname{Res}\operatorname{tr}((dA)B)\) yields \([e_2,f_2]=-h_1+K\). Using \(\operatorname{Res}\operatorname{tr}(A\,dB)\) instead yields \(-h_1-K\). Either convention defines the central extension, but the displayed bracket and \(h_2\) must agree.',r'This is the loop realization of the affine algebra, already used in the construction summarized by \citet{lepowskywilson1978construction}; see also \citet[Chapter 7]{kac1983infinite}. The sign discrepancy is checked directly by differentiating \(t^{-1}\).',('lepowskywilson1978construction','kac1983infinite'),literal='false as written',reconstruction='The residue convention is fixed explicitly; replacing the cocycle sign is an emendation, not a different historical claim.')
add(561,'Root monomials and the proposal to make paths continuous','P001028','question',r'Weights count occurrences of the \(e_j\) in a monomial. A staircase path is drawn, followed by \ru{как сделать, чтобы пути были непрерывны?}',r'A Lie word has multidegree given by its generator multiplicities. The question about continuous paths specifies neither a topology, a limiting parameter, nor which algebraic operations the path model must preserve; no unique mathematical problem can be recovered.',r'Comparison with the published affine construction and Kac\textquotesingle s representation framework yields no exact target. Later path models cannot be identified with this sentence merely from the word ``paths\textquotesingle\textquotesingle.',('lepowskywilson1978construction','kac1983infinite'),cl='F',literal='not determinable',match='none found',verification='unresolved lead',reconstruction='Only the multigrading is definite. No Littelmann-path or stochastic-path theorem is imported.',confidence='low',speaker='I. M. Gelfand',status='the multigrading is standard, while the continuous-path request remains underdetermined as a historical item.')
add(561,'The basic highest-weight module','P001029','construction',r'A cyclic vector satisfies \(e_1v_0=e_2v_0=0\), \(h_1v_0=0\), \(h_2v_0=v_0\). Its space is \(\mathbb C[x_1,x_3,x_5,\ldots]\).',r'For the affine algebra with \(K=h_1+h_2\), the irreducible integrable highest-weight module of weight \(\Lambda\) with \(\Lambda(h_1)=0\), \(\Lambda(h_2)=1\) has level one and the principal bosonic realization on the polynomial algebra in positive odd variables. The Verma module with these highest weights must first be quotiented by its maximal proper submodule.',r'Exactly the odd-variable realization is identified by the original abstract of \citet{lepowskywilson1978construction}, published August 1978. The distinction between Verma and irreducible integrable modules is essential.',('lepowskywilson1978construction',),match='exact',reconstruction='Irreducibility, integrability, level and the quotient qualification make the notebook\textquotesingle s ``most economical\textquotesingle\textquotesingle precise.')
add(561,'Nonconjugate loop Cartans and the square-root obstruction','P001029','claim',r'After quotienting by the center, diagonal loops and matrices \(\left(\begin{smallmatrix}0&f(t)\\tf(t)&0\end{smallmatrix}\right)\) form nonconjugate commutative subalgebras. Pointwise diagonalization is possible, but continuous diagonalization is not.',r'For \(t\in S^1\), \(B(t)=\left(\begin{smallmatrix}0&1\\t&0\end{smallmatrix}\right)\) has distinct eigenvalues \(\pm\sqrt t\). A continuous periodic diagonalization with labeled diagonal entries would give a continuous square root of \(t\), impossible since its winding number would be one half. Over \(\mathbb C[t,t^{-1}]\) this likewise obstructs conjugation to the split diagonal Cartan.',r'The principal Heisenberg in \citet{lepowskywilson1978construction} implements this distinction. The winding-number explanation supplied here is an elementary reconstruction of the specific notebook example.',('lepowskywilson1978construction',),literal='correct',match='partial',reconstruction='The domain S1, complex coefficient field, and nonvanishing choice f=1 are specified; no obstruction is claimed on a simply connected arc.')
add(561,'A p-adic analogy without a specified statement','P001029','remark',r'Gelfand says that ``this algebra\textquotesingle\textquotesingle arises naturally in the \(p\)-adic case.',r'The sentence does not specify a local field, a group, a building, or a representation. Affine root systems occur in several inequivalent \(p\)-adic constructions; the intended assertion is not determined.',r'The nearby loop-algebra context and earlier affine/building entries were compared, but they do not select one statement. The remark is not evidence of an unsolved classification.',(),cl='F',literal='not determinable',match='none found',verification='unresolved lead',confidence='low',speaker='I. M. Gelfand',status='the historical referent remains unidentified.')
add(561,'Quadratic forms and an unspecified count of 2 to the n','P001029','remark',r'Gelfand mentions Mishchenko and quadratic forms: \ru{количество \(2^n\), но кан. виды не описаны}.',r'No ground field, coefficient ring, equivalence relation or meaning of \(n\) is supplied. Consequently the count \(2^n\) is not a well-defined classification claim.',r'Neither the cited Lepowsky--Wilson setting nor the supplied earlier-year index supplies these missing data. No later quadratic-form classification is equated with this allusion.',(),cl='F',literal='not determinable',match='none found',verification='unresolved lead',confidence='low',speaker='I. M. Gelfand',status='unidentified; a scan or other record specifying the forms would be needed before research development.')
add(561,'Principal Heisenberg modes and the Fock representation','P001029','construction',r'\(B_{2k+1}=\left(\begin{smallmatrix}0&t^k\\t^{k+1}&0\end{smallmatrix}\right)\), with \([B_{2k+1},B_{2l+1}]=\delta(k+l)(2l+1)\mathbf1\), is followed by multiplication/differentiation operators and an irreducibility assertion.',r'For the printed cocycle \(c(A,B)=\operatorname{Res}\operatorname{tr}(A\,dB)\), direct multiplication gives \([B_{2k+1},B_{2l+1}]=(2l+1)\delta_{k+l+1,0}K\). Abstractly, modes with \([a_m,a_n]=m\delta_{m+n,0}\) act for positive odd \(m\) by \(a_m=\partial_{x_m}\), \(a_{-m}=m x_m\) on polynomials; the vacuum is 1 and the representation is irreducible.',r'The Heisenberg restriction is the standard oscillator component of \citet{lepowskywilson1978construction}. The missing shift in the Kronecker delta and mixed variable indices must be repaired independently of its normalization.',('lepowskywilson1978construction',),literal='false as written',reconstruction='The Fock-mode notation is normalized separately from the notebook\textquotesingle s inconsistent signs; positive modes annihilate the highest-weight vacuum.')
add(561,'Exponential modes realize the remaining affine generators','P001029','method',r'The notes form \(L=e^{\sum x_k}e^{4\sum\partial_{x_k}}=\sum L_m\), with weighted homogeneous components, and express \(C_{2k+1}\) and \(H_{2k}\) through them.',r'The principal realization extends the Heisenberg action on \(\mathbb C[x_1,x_3,\ldots]\) to the basic affine module using coefficients of a normally ordered formal exponential field. Each coefficient acts on a polynomial through finitely many derivative terms; the multiplication part is interpreted in the graded completion. The coefficients and grading must be chosen together to satisfy the affine brackets.',r'This is the specific construction described in \citet[pp.~43--53]{lepowskywilson1978construction}. Publisher abstract verification establishes the match; it does not verify the notebook\textquotesingle s coefficient 4 or recover its omitted spectral parameter.',('lepowskywilson1978construction',),match='exact',reconstruction='The formal-series domain and completion are added; no unverified numerical normalization is promoted to an exact operator formula.',confidence='medium')
corr('P001027','Generalized Cartan conditions and relation (2)',r'\(a_{ij}<0\), and \(e_i^{1-a_{ij}}e_j=f_i^{1-a_{ij}}f_j=0\).',r'Allow \(a_{ij}=0\) for disconnected vertices; write adjoint powers for \(i\ne j\).','Scan inspected: strict inequality and omission of ad are present in the handwriting. These are mathematical emendations, not mistranscriptions.')
corr('P001027','Finite/affine positivity criterion',r'Positivity of \((a_{ij})\) without a symmetrizer.',r'For indecomposable symmetrizable A test the symmetric matrix DA with D positive diagonal.','The displayed B2 and G2 matrices are nonsymmetric. Scan and Russian agree; the qualification is necessary.')
corr('P001028','First affine matrix',r'\(\left(\begin{smallmatrix}2&-2\\-2&-2\end{smallmatrix}\right)\).',r'\(\left(\begin{smallmatrix}2&-2\\-2&2\end{smallmatrix}\right)\).','Scan inspected: lower-right -2 is clear. Kirillov repeats the correct +2 matrix lower on the same page.')
corr('P001028','Loop cocycle versus h2',r'\(+\operatorname{Res}\operatorname{tr}(A\,dB)K\) and \(h_2=-h_1+K\).',r'Change the cocycle to \(\operatorname{Res}\operatorname{tr}((dA)B)K\), or change h2 to -h1-K.','Scan inspected; differentiation of t^{-1} gives central term -K with the printed convention.')
corr('P001029','Principal Heisenberg bracket',r'\(\delta(k+l)(2l+1)K\).',r'\(\delta_{k+l+1,0}(2l+1)K\) for the printed cocycle.','Scan inspected. tr(B_{2k+1}dB_{2l+1})=(2l+1)t^{k+l}dt, so the residue condition is k+l=-1.')
corr('P001029','Oscillator action indices and vacuum',r'Positive B modes multiply; negative modes differentiate; indices alternate between x_k and x_{2k+1}.',r'Fix one indexing convention and match raising/annihilation operators to the sign of the chosen B modes and highest-weight vector.','Scan inspected. For the highest-weight convention, B1=e1+e2 annihilates v0, so it cannot act as multiplication by a nonzero variable on the vacuum 1.')
audit.append('## Record561\nSource boundary verified: P001026–29; Russian P001027–29 read and scans1027,1028,1029 inspected. Opened Kac1968 Math-Net metadata, Kac1983 publisher contents, Lepowsky–Wilson1978 publisher abstract. First-page/section bibliography chronology keeps1978 exposition E. Old index links: 1976-408.16 and1981-532.5 are thematic recurrences, not definite problem identities. No precise open problem recoverable from continuous-path, p-adic, or2^n remarks. Direct residue and winding checks performed independently.')
